\par }{\fs20\lang1024\langfe1024\noproof {\shp{\*\shpinst\shpleft1440\shptop2070\shpright10800\shpbottom2070\shpfhdr1\shpbxpage\shpbxignore\shpbypage\shpbyignore\shpwr3\shpwrk0\shpfblwtxt0\shpz2\shplockanchor\shplid2049{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 20}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn shapePath}{\sv 4}}{\sp{\sn fFillOK}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFilled}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fArrowheadsOK}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelh}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn posrelv}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}{\shprslt{\*\do\dobxpage\dobypage\dodhgt8194\dpline\dpptx0\dppty0\dpptx9920\dppty0\dpx1190\dpy2070\dpxsize9920\dpysize0\dplinew15\dplinecor0\dplinecog0\dplinecob0}}}}{\f0\fs16  \par }}{\footerf \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }{\footer \pard\plain \s22\ql \b\f354\fs18  Page {\field{\*\fldinst PAGE}{\fldrslt 1}} of {\field{\*\fldinst NUMPAGES}{\fldrslt 1}}{     }\'a9 2026 \uc2 Factiva, Inc.  All rights reserved.\par }\pard\plain \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\fs20 {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 07:30 HALF-HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 541 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ABORTION, LAW, SUSPENSION, TEXAS, APPEAL\par \par \uc2 FLOODING, RESCUE\par \par \uc2 SHOOTING, SIMPKINS, SCHOOL, HARRISON, KOLBYE\par \par \uc2 OIL SPILL, INVESTIGATION, WILSHER\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: NEW IMAGES OF CRACKED OIL PIPELINE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SHOWS RUPTURE THAT CAUSED UP TO, 144,000 GALLONS OF OIL TO SPILL\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, MANDATES, VACCINES, FLU\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: LOS ANGELES VACCINE CRACKDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: CITY ENACTS ONE OF NATION'S STRICTEST MANDATES\par \par \uc2 DEBT, DEAL, SENATE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK FROM THE BRINK?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: SENATE NEARS DEAL TO AVERT GOVERNMENT DEFAULT\par \par \uc2 MLB, PLAYOFFS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WILD CARD WALKOFF!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DODGERS BEAT CARDINALS WITH GAME-WINNING HOME RUN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Back here on "GMA," yeah, she is simply the best. We're talking about Tina Turner, ladies and gentlemen. And you know what, the legendary pop diva, she has made a blockbuster deal with a major music company. We're talking, we're talking, we'll tell you all the details coming up in "Pop News." Can we just go outside for a little bit? Great group that's outside. That one woman to the right with the black shirt on, she's from the ATL Rhonda (PH). She said she used to listen to me on the V103 (inaudible) in the morning. Yeah. And I said, what, was she in her crib when she was watching me or listening to me on the radio? I mean, how was, that was back in the '80s.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I love when you take it back. I love it when you take it back to the radio voice.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And she loved it as well.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She did as well, George.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 She did.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: ABORTION BAN BLOCKED\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 We have a lot of headlines we're following this morning, including, of course, that federal judge who's ruled in favor of the Biden administration to block the enforcement of the new Texas abortion law, the most restrictive in the nation that banned nearly all abortions in the state.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FLASH FLOOD EMERGENCY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And the flash flood emergency threatening the southeast. More than ten inches of rain have drenched Alabama overnight. Emergency rescue crews are working to rescue people stranded in the flood. Six states are now under flood watches.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRAMATIC DASHCAM VIDEO\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And look at this dramatic dashcam video from Virginia. An out-of-control car slamming into a police cruiser, barely missing two officers. Officer Matthew Stewart pulling his colleague to safety just in time.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Oh, wow.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Thank goodness he was alert. And we've got a lot more ahead, including a home heating alert.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: WHAT'S NEXT\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Prices expected to skyrocket this winter. How to keep warm and save money. Becky Worley is gonna tell us that. And we are ready to "Rise & Shine" in beautiful Wisconsin this morning. We are celebrating the beauty of the state and the resilience of the people of the Badger State. That is coming up, Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 I love how you say, "Rise & Shine."\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 "Rise & Shine."\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211023eha70000a\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 TEXAS ABORTION LAW BLOCKED FEDERAL JUDGE PAUSES LAW BANNING MOST ABORTIONS IN TX\b0\par\par\uc2 823 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: World News Tonight with David Muir\par \uc2 WNT\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WALENSKY, COVID-19, \uc2 PFIZER\uc2 , BIDEN, FLU, WALTER\par \par \uc2 ABORTION LAW, MILLER, ENFORCEMENT, APPEAL, PITMAN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION LAW BLOCKED\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And now to that battle over the controversial new Texas law that had halted nearly all abortions in that state. Overnight, a federal judge temporarily blocking enforcement of that new law in a 113-page ruling. The judge saying the new law is flagrantly unconstitutional. Tonight, Texas promptly filing an appeal. So, where does this go from here? And why many clinics are hesitant to reopen in that state. Tonight, Rachel Scott with the story of one young woman and her difficult decision, her journey in the middle of all this.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: FEDERAL JUDGE PAUSES LAW BANNING MOST ABORTIONS IN TX\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Tonight, in Texas, supporters of abortion rights cheering the federal judge's ruling, putting a temporary hold on the most restrictive abortion law in the land.\par \par \uc2 AMY HAGSTROM MILLER (WHOLE WOMAN'S HEALTH)\par \par \uc2 We reached out to some of the patients that we had on a waiting list to come in to have abortions today.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TEXAS ABORTION LAW\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The law bans abortion after about six weeks of pregnancy, and it deputizes everyday citizens to file lawsuits against anyone they say "aids or abets" an abortion, from the doctor who performs the procedure to the Uber driver who takes the woman to a clinic. And if they win, they get a bounty of at least $10,000. But now, as legal challenges make their way through the courts, Judge Robert Pitman putting the law on pause, ruling that because of its "unprecedented and aggressive scheme, women have been unlawfully prevented from exercising control over their lives in ways that are protected by the Constitution." And since the law went into effect, most Texas women seeking abortions have had to leave the state to get one. I sat down with Maddie, a 21-year-old college student, the day before she traveled to Mississippi for the procedure.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) At six weeks, you didn't even know you were pregnant?\par \par \uc2 WOMAN SEEKING ABORTION (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Not even close. I was still living my life as regular and as carefree of a college kid as I could be.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She was on birth control, but by the time she took a pregnancy test and went to the doctor, it was too late to get an abortion, under Texas law.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN SEEKING ABORTION (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 When she told me that I was measuring at 10-and-a-half weeks, I just cried. I was heartbroken.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Did it sink in in that moment that you would have to travel hundreds of miles to get an abortion procedure, if you wanted to?\par \par \uc2 WOMAN SEEKING ABORTION (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah. The minute that they said how far along I was, I knew that this became 100 times more difficult, more expensive, and more time-consuming.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Maddie started calling around to clinics in nearby states.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) How many clinics would you say you called altogether?\par \par \uc2 WOMAN SEEKING ABORTION (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Easily 30, if not more.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And most of them were booked.\par \par \uc2 WOMAN SEEKING ABORTION (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 Yeah.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She finally got an appointment in Mississippi. But when she got there, she was told that they have a mandatory waiting period. She had to go back to Texas and return to Mississippi the following week for the actual procedure. Two separate trips.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) What message do you have for the Texas lawmakers who backed this law?\par \par \uc2 WOMAN SEEKING ABORTION (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 My body is not their property. They should have no say in what I do with myself. I am in charges of myself, in every possible way.\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And Rachel Scott joins us live, tonight, from Houston. And, Rachel, this law now on pause, but it's just one judge's ruling. The state of Texas now appealing this decision. Where does it go from here?\par \par \uc2 RACHEL SCOTT (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Well, David, the Texas attorney general says this boils down to the sanctity of human life. He is appealing this to the Fifth Circuit. That is known to be one of the most conservative courts in the country. It could find itself in front of the Supreme Court. And even now, abortion providers in this state are hesitant to fully resume abortion procedures. One telling me tonight, they cannot afford to take the chance. David?\par \par \uc2 DAVID MUIR (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Rachel Scott live in Houston, tonight. Rachel, thank you. And I know Rachel will have much more of her interview in a reporting project for "Nightline" that will air next week.\par \par \uc2 Document WNT0000020211008eha700003\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 DRAGON DREAM TEAM BREAST CANCER SURVIVORS ON A MISSION\b0\par\par\uc2 1,500 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, OIL SPILL, NGUYEN, ORE\par \par \uc2 SOCIAL MEDIA, OUTAGE, \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 , HAUGEN, MADORY, PSAKI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2  BACK ONLINE AFTER MAJOR OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLIONS IMPACTED AS APPS INCLUDING INSTAGRAM & WHATSAPP GO OFFLINE FOR HOURS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DEBT CEILING, INFRASTRUCTURE, BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT'S NEW WARNING AS DEBT DEFAULT DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN: "I CAN'T" GUARANTEE U.S. WILL PAY DEBTS DESPITE "DIRE" CONSEQUENCES\par \par \uc2 AMTRAK\uc2 , SHOOTING, INVESTIGATION, MAGNUS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY \uc2 AMTRAK\uc2  SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNMAN OPENS FIRE, KILLING DEA AGENT & WOUNDING TWO OTHERS\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, FAUCI, CDC, MANDATES\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL, WILD CARD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 YANKEES\uc2  & \uc2 RED SOX\uc2  FACE OFF IN WILD CARD GAME\par \par \uc2 WALLACE, NASCAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "NO TIME TO DIE"\par \par \uc2 PETITO, LAUNDRIE, INVESTIGATION, DAVIS, DEPAUL\par \par \uc2 SPACE, TRAVEL, RUSSIA, ANDERSON, SHATNER, FILM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE NEW SPACE RACE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIA ROCKET BLASTS OFF ON MISSION TO MAKE FIRST FEATURE FILM IN SPACE\par \par \uc2 HALLOWEEN, "THE MATRIX", LIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 OIL, SPILL, EMERGENCY, NGUYEN\par \par \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 , INSTAGRAM, WHATSAPP, OFFLINE, OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON & JOHNSON\uc2 , BOOSTER, FDA, PROTECTION, CDC\par \par \uc2 "DANCING WITH THE STARS," NEW KIDS ON THE BLOCK, SHAQ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRAMA IN THE BALLROOM!\par \par \uc2 "ANNE WITH AN E," MCKEON, CANCER, TEPLINSKY, PATEL\par \par \uc2 TUCCI, FOOD, RECIPES, "TASTE", MEMOIR, COOKING\par \par \uc2 CRAIG, "NO TIME TO DIE", BOND\par \par \uc2 FOX, PANTUSO, DONNELY, BREAST CANCER, DRAGON\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) We're back now on "GMA" with women from Ohio who are on a mission to fight breast cancer one stroke at a time. Janai Norman is on the water with the Dragon Dream team and they are all together in pink and looking good. Good morning, Janai.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Robin, good morning. These women are not just survivors, they are thrivers. They are the definition of strength and perseverance. And out here on the water is where they found hope and community and their mission to increase self-esteem and physical and emotional well-being through paddling. And when you see them out on the water, you see they do exactly that and so much more.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) They're strangers turned sisters.\par \par \uc2 OBSERVER (FEMALE)\par \par \uc2 They're very competitive.\par \par \uc2 ALLEN (DRAGON DREAM TEAM COACH)\par \par \uc2 They don't look like a lot but when you put them on the water, they're amazing on the water.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Athletes linked arm in arm who call themselves...\par \par \uc2 DRAGON DREAM TEAM MEMBERS (GROUP)\par \par \uc2 Dragon Dream team.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) These fierce warriors bonded by their shared experience with breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 SUSAN (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Cancer was no longer gonna control us, even though it's always in the back of your mind. It's always haunting you and this was a way for us to control that.\par \par \uc2 DEANN (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 You start hearing about everybody's story and how it relates to you, we're all in the same boat but every story is different so it makes it kind of nice.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) The dragon boat holds 22 in all, 20 paddlers plus a steer person and a drummer. That role played by 84-year-old Pat.\par \par \uc2 ALLEN (DRAGON DREAM TEAM COACH)\par \par \uc2 The vast majority of them have never been on an athletic team in their lives, so this is their first opportunity to really come out and compete in an athletic sport.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) And all that paddling, not so easy. Take it from the newest member, Drusilla.\par \par \uc2 DRUSILLA (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 I was prepared for the upper body workout but it's a full-body workout. You know, I wasn't prepared for that.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At races like this one out in Pittsburgh, the real prize for some found in moments like this, ceremonies for the survivors allowing for an embrace and some tears. But let's be clear, these ladies came for the gold.\par \par \uc2 DEANN (BREAST CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 There's nothing like competition, in my opinion. We all have the same common goal. Be winners.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Round after round, the team scoring victories leading to this final match-up, an epic three-way race. With drummer Pat at the helm, the Dragon Dream team paddling ahead of the competition. And, if you couldn't guess by now, they won.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) How cool is that? We've got a couple of these - we've got the whole team here, basically, but a couple of the women right here with us. We've got Pat, Davida and Barb. Guys, ladies, this is a tough sport. I was out there on the water with you this morning. My back and shoulders are gonna hurt tomorrow. How'd you think I did?\par \par \uc2 PAT DONNELY (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, I thought you were grand.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah? I'll take it.\par \par \uc2 BARB FOX (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 You are a born natural. Born.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Thank you\u8230\'20\'26\par \par \uc2 DAVIDA PANTUSO (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Awesome.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...very much. So you would, you would draft me first round pick (inaudible) ...\par \par \uc2 DAVIDA PANTUSO (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 BARB FOX (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Oh, yeah, you're on board.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) So, Pat, you're one of the original team members. You were paddling for over a decade. Now you are the heart and soul, the heartbeat beating your drum to keep the team all paddling in time. How has your role with the team changed?\par \par \uc2 PAT DONNELY (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Well, now I feel like I've become more of a cheerleader and I've tried to encourage them and keep them in sync. That's the hardest part. But keeping them in sync and I relate to them what the coach says, because that's a long boat and you can't always hear in the front, so I relay the information. And, of course, we are all wanting to win so I just try to cheer them on, say those things that - make them wanna...\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...keep them motivated.\par \par \uc2 PAT DONNELY (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 ...go faster (inaudible)...\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Davida, you're one of the youngest members of the team. You said you used to do yoga that helped keep your mind, body and spirit altogether. But after a devastating diagnosis, it was hard for you to get everything in sync again.\par \par \uc2 DAVIDA PANTUSO (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Right, absolutely. So after you go through cancer, you have a lot of healing to do. And I like to compare this to my doctor's healing my physical body, obviously. And then my, my husband's, my husband and our families and our friends, they definitely helped me heal emotionally from this experience. But I wasn't myself. It wasn't until I came out here and I took that paddle and I took my first paddle forward that I knew my spirit, the essence of who I was, was coming back. And when the boat moved forward, I knew I was moving forward with my life and living a full, active, thriving and happy life again.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) That is incredible. And I could see how it is so therapeutic and meditative out there on the water.\par \par \uc2 DAVIDA PANTUSO (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Absolutely.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And, Barb, you were helping women across the state of Ohio who have been diagnosed with breast cancer giving them pashminas. So you've not only been a part of this community on the water, but out and about in the community. When you see women with those scarves, what's that mean to you? How's that feel?\par \par \uc2 BARB FOX (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 So for us as a team, we know that we're out there helping, just like what Davida said, getting people back into the world, get people back into their old lives. Showing them a new life so they can move forward and be a part of the big picture and get things done and get breast cancer, just get rid of it. So get your mammogram.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Get your mammogram. There you go, (inaudible) today. Well, ladies, our friends at Walgreens heard about your team, the incredible things you guys are doing. They wanted to celebrate you so they are giving each of you beauty products to help you feel like you, but that's not all. They are also donating $10,000. How exciting is that?\par \par \uc2 PAT DONNELY (CANCER SURVIVOR)\par \par \uc2 Awesome.\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Congratulations. Guys, back to you.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) All right. Janai, thank you. Thank you for sharing that. That is amazing. That's some serious (inaudible) right there.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Yeah.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Very worthy.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Fantastic.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Now, let's check in with Ginger again. Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211021eha50003h\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 "ANNE WITH AN E" STAR'S CANCER BATTLE MIRANDA MCKEON SHARES HER JOURNEY AT 19 YEARS OLD\b0\par\par\uc2 846 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, OIL SPILL, NGUYEN, ORE\par \par \uc2 SOCIAL MEDIA, OUTAGE, \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 , HAUGEN, MADORY, PSAKI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2  BACK ONLINE AFTER MAJOR OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLIONS IMPACTED AS APPS INCLUDING INSTAGRAM & WHATSAPP GO OFFLINE FOR HOURS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DEBT CEILING, INFRASTRUCTURE, BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT'S NEW WARNING AS DEBT DEFAULT DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN: "I CAN'T" GUARANTEE U.S. WILL PAY DEBTS DESPITE "DIRE" CONSEQUENCES\par \par \uc2 AMTRAK\uc2 , SHOOTING, INVESTIGATION, MAGNUS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY \uc2 AMTRAK\uc2  SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNMAN OPENS FIRE, KILLING DEA AGENT & WOUNDING TWO OTHERS\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, FAUCI, CDC, MANDATES\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL, WILD CARD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 YANKEES\uc2  & \uc2 RED SOX\uc2  FACE OFF IN WILD CARD GAME\par \par \uc2 WALLACE, NASCAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "NO TIME TO DIE"\par \par \uc2 PETITO, LAUNDRIE, INVESTIGATION, DAVIS, DEPAUL\par \par \uc2 SPACE, TRAVEL, RUSSIA, ANDERSON, SHATNER, FILM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE NEW SPACE RACE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIA ROCKET BLASTS OFF ON MISSION TO MAKE FIRST FEATURE FILM IN SPACE\par \par \uc2 HALLOWEEN, "THE MATRIX", LIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 OIL, SPILL, EMERGENCY, NGUYEN\par \par \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 , INSTAGRAM, WHATSAPP, OFFLINE, OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON & JOHNSON\uc2 , BOOSTER, FDA, PROTECTION, CDC\par \par \uc2 "DANCING WITH THE STARS," NEW KIDS ON THE BLOCK, SHAQ\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRAMA IN THE BALLROOM!\par \par \uc2 "ANNE WITH AN E," MCKEON, CANCER, TEPLINSKY, PATEL\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) But now our "GMA" Cover Story. The "Anne With An E" actress living with stage 3 breast cancer at just 19 years old. The young actress spoke with Kaylee Hartung about the challenges she's facing and how she's staying positive. Good morning, Kaylee.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Hey, good morning, Robin. When Miranda first felt this unusual lump in her breast she jumped down a \uc2 Google\uc2  rabbit hole. She convinced herself it can't be, no way, it can't be cancer. She thought, I'm just 19. But still she went to a doctor to advocate for her health.\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 Hey, everyone. So this is what life looks like, round four of chemo.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Miranda McKeon never imagined this was the story she'd be sharing.\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 I did cold capping.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) At just 19 years old, the "Anne With An E" actress felt an unusual lump in her breast.\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 I have stage 3 breast cancer.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Women younger than 40 account for just about four percent of breast cancer cases in the US and Miranda is one of them.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR ELEONORA TEPLINSKY (ONCOLOGIST AND SUPPORT FOR MIRANDA)\par \par \uc2 The young woman diagnosed with breast cancer struggled with fertility, pregnancy concerns, body image, financial toxicity.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) Before her treatment could even begin, she said her doctors presented her with an important decision.\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 It was explained to me that with chemotherapy treatment there is risks of infertility down the line and fertility was not something that I had ever considered.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (VO) She quickly began the regimen of hormone injections and froze her eggs.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Have the conversations about a treatment plan for a 19-year-old been different than if you were older?\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 The treatment is still the same protocol for my type of hormone-positive cancer.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) It takes what it takes...\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 Yes.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...to fight cancer, no matter your age.\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 That's true. I am spending every other Tuesday in the clinic while my friends are at class. I'd rather be in class, but this is my job right now.\par \par \uc2 DOCTOR NIKI PATEL (MIRANDA MCKEON'S ONCOLOGIST)\par \par \uc2 Miranda has an aggressive tumor, but she has, at the end of the day, a curable tumor, and so she is knee-deep in aggressive chemotherapy.\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 I think I've put my head down and been like, you know what, we're going to keep this on a positive track because it could go dark quickly, but that's not where I need to be living.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Because the key word there is living.\par \par \uc2 MIRANDA MCKEON (ACTRESS BATTLING CANCER)\par \par \uc2 Yes, and living well.\par \par \uc2 KAYLEE HARTUNG (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) And next week Miranda will complete her final round of chemo. With surgeries and radiation ahead, she knows the fight is far from over, but she is looking ahead to a full life, getting back to acting, her next semester at USC and farther down the road there is that hope for a family. Robin.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Oh, good for her. Just her, her perseverance and getting out there and telling the story because at 19 you don't think that's going to happen to you with breast cancer. Kaylee, thank you so much for that enlightening time with Miranda. We appreciate it. Now let's go back to Ginger. Ginger.\par \par \uc2 Document GMA0000020211021eha50003c\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 INTRODUCTION TO THE 8:00 HALF HOUR\b0\par\par\uc2 708 \uc2 words\par \uc2 5 October 2021\par \uc2 ABC News: Good Morning America\par \uc2 GMA\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 \u169\'00\'A9 Copyright 2021, American Broadcasting Companies, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 INVESTIGATION, OIL SPILL, NGUYEN, ORE\par \par \uc2 SOCIAL MEDIA, OUTAGE, \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2 , HAUGEN, MADORY, PSAKI\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 FACEBOOK\uc2  BACK ONLINE AFTER MAJOR OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BILLIONS IMPACTED AS APPS INCLUDING INSTAGRAM & WHATSAPP GO OFFLINE FOR HOURS\par \par \uc2 BIDEN, DEBT CEILING, INFRASTRUCTURE, BILL\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PRESIDENT'S NEW WARNING AS DEBT DEFAULT DEADLINE LOOMS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BIDEN: "I CAN'T" GUARANTEE U.S. WILL PAY DEBTS DESPITE "DIRE" CONSEQUENCES\par \par \uc2 AMTRAK\uc2 , SHOOTING, INVESTIGATION, MAGNUS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DEADLY \uc2 AMTRAK\uc2  SHOOTING\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GUNMAN OPENS FIRE, KILLING DEA AGENT & WOUNDING TWO OTHERS\par \par \uc2 COVID-19, VACCINES, FAUCI, CDC, MANDATES\par \par \uc2 BASEBALL, WILD CARD\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DO OR DIE SHOWDOWN\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: \uc2 YANKEES\uc2  & \uc2 RED SOX\uc2  FACE OFF IN WILD CARD GAME\par \par \uc2 WALLACE, NASCAR\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: GOOD MORNING AMERICA\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RIGHT NOW\par \par \uc2 CLIP FROM MOVIE, "NO TIME TO DIE"\par \par \uc2 PETITO, LAUNDRIE, INVESTIGATION, DAVIS, DEPAUL\par \par \uc2 SPACE, TRAVEL, RUSSIA, ANDERSON, SHATNER, FILM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: THE NEW SPACE RACE?\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: RUSSIA ROCKET BLASTS OFF ON MISSION TO MAKE FIRST FEATURE FILM IN SPACE\par \par \uc2 HALLOWEEN, "THE MATRIX", LIGHTS\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: PLAY OF THE DAY\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Good morning, America, it's 8:00 AM. State of emergency. The race to contain the oil disaster. This morning, new questions over when officials first knew about the spill. Why was there a 12-hour delay to shut the pipeline as investigators close in on a possible cause of the rupture.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MAJOR SOCIAL MEDIA OUTAGE\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BACK ONLINE\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 The massive outage for \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and WhatsApp. Back online after disrupting billions of users worldwide. This morning, what the company and Mark Zuckerberg are saying about the chaos.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: MIRANDA MCKEON'S BREAST CANCER BATTLE\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 At just 19 years old, she's living with stage 3 breast cancer. The "Anne With An E" actress sharing her challenges on TikTok and the tough decisions she faced when it came to the future of her fertility before her treatment could even begin.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: BRITNEY NIGHT IN THE BALLROOM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: "DANCING WITH THE STARS"\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Dancing does it again. The stars spinning into Britney night in the ballroom. Three leading ladies at the top of the leaderboard. Plus, how did Cody and Cheryl pull off their performance from home? And which duo got the boot.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DANIEL CRAIG, LIVE!\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: JAMES BOND IS BACK\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Countdown to "No Time To Die." It's Bond week on "GMA."\par \par \uc2 RALPH FIENNES ("NO TIME TO DIE")\par \par \uc2 Where's 007?\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 Daniel Craig is here ahead of his final bow as...\par \par \uc2 DANIEL CRAIG ("NO TIME TO DIE")\par \par \uc2 James Bond.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 He's joining us live in Times Square.\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: DRAGON DREAM TEAM\par \par \uc2 GRAPHICS: TOGETHER IN PINK\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 And a boatload of hope. Meet the Dragon Dream Team fighting breast cancer one stroke at a time, thriving on the water. This morning, they join us live together in pink. And they're saying...\par \par \uc2 JANAI NORMAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Good morning, America.\par \par \uc2 ANNOUNCER\par \par \uc2 Live in Times Square, this is "GMA."\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Tina Turner on a Tuesday morning. Good morning, America. Great to be with me boys, Michael and George here in Times Square. And Janai Norman is having an amazing morning in Ohio. Look at her.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Look at that smile.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Wouldn't you be? Look, the Dragon Dream Team is with her. Cannot wait to hear more from these women thriving on the water and how they're helping their community, as well. We've got a big surprise for them coming up.\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) They are in unison. And it was two years ago this month that the "GMA" Book Club was born. Three million copies in print, 24 page turners, 16 of them instant "The \uc2 New York Times\uc2 " bestsellers, and this morning we've got one more for October.\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Okay, let's give it up for our book club...\par \par \uc2 MICHAEL STRAHAN (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) (Inaudible).\par \par \uc2 ROBIN ROBERTS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) ...they have done a tremendous job. They really have, all the way around. Yeah.\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS (ABC NEWS)\par \par \uc2 (\uc2 OC\uc2 ) Great job, it's been a great idea.\par \par \uc2 Docu